From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:58:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] AROS: joysticks through controller.hidd

A jsJoystick backend for AROS's game controller subsystem (controller.hidd,
fed by the USB HID class). The OOP calls are in C (jsAROS_hidd.c); the C++
side (jsAROS.cxx) only fills in the class.

Joystick numbers: a controller keeps its number while it is there, and a
controller that has no number yet takes the lowest free one, whichever
joystick object is being opened. FlightGear re-opens every joystick that
does not work once a second, 16 of them; without that rule a stick that
comes back is given to whichever of them asks first, usually one that has
no bindings.

Axes are numbered as Linux's joydev numbers a HID device's (X, Y, Z, Rx,
Ry, Rz, throttle, rudder, wheel, gas, brake, then the rest), followed by
two axes per hat, and the name is "Maker Product": that is what FGData's
joystick files match on and count in (<unix>). Axis values are what the
controller subsystem hands out, -32767..32767 with its own dead zone; an
axis with one direction is spread over the same range. The first 32
buttons are passed on.
